LRC pair-cell operation-grid Tournament Analysis
====================================================================================================
Tie Hamiltonian path: lexicographic pair-cell order (0,1)->(0,2)->... .
Strict arcs compare pair-cell scalar values; equal values use the tie path.

Pair-cell criteria:
  edge_danger_deficit       dynamic=True  observable=pair-cell deficit max(0,1/n-dist(i,j,t))
    switch=larger current LRC danger deficit points to smaller deficit
  edge_phase_distance       dynamic=True  observable=pair-cell circular distance dist(i,j,t)
    switch=larger distance points to smaller distance
  edge_wall_frequency       dynamic=False observable=pair-cell speed gap |v_i-v_j|
    switch=larger half-turn wall frequency points to smaller frequency
  edge_dyadic_row           dynamic=False observable=dyadic row v2(|v_i-v_j|)
    switch=higher x*2 branch row points to lower row
  edge_odd_core             dynamic=False observable=odd core of |v_i-v_j| on the x+2 row
    switch=smaller odd core points to larger odd core
  edge_same_odd_chain       dynamic=False observable=whether both speeds lie on the same odd-core doubling chain
    switch=same-chain and deeper-row pairs point to other pairs
  edge_product_sum_defect   dynamic=False observable=residue-pair distance from (a-1)(b-1)=n-1
    switch=closer product-sum critical pair points to farther pair

